Scope and third-party material

This license covers the original materials authored by Adri M in this
repository: the HTML/CSS/JS of the Manifiesto Caníbal pages, the run-of-show
(guión) and the printable discussion handout, and the accompanying texts. The
seminar activity is meant to be reproduced and adapted by others under these
terms.

It does NOT extend to:
  - Francis Picabia, "Manifeste cannibale dada" (1920), and Oswald de Andrade,
    "Manifesto Antropófago" (1928): quoted for commentary, criticism and
    teaching; rights remain with their respective holders / the public domain
    as applicable in your jurisdiction.
  - The optional background audio bed (audio/canibal-bed.mp3): a non-commercial
    transformative remix made under s.29.21 of the Canadian Copyright Act;
    sources are credited on the page.
  - Third-party fonts (Google Fonts: Anton, Spectral, Space Mono), under their
    own licenses (SIL Open Font License).
